<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>HugeGraph-AI on Apache HugeGraph</title><link>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/</link><description>Recent content in HugeGraph-AI on Apache HugeGraph</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-US</language><lastBuildDate>Wed, 02 Sep 2026 18:46:24 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>HugeGraph-LLM</title><link>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/hugegraph-llm/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/hugegraph-llm/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Please refer to the AI repository &lt;a href="https://github.com/apache/hugegraph-ai/tree/main/hugegraph-llm#readme"&gt;README&lt;/a&gt; for the most up-to-date documentation, and the official website &lt;strong&gt;regularly&lt;/strong&gt; is updated and synchronized.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bridge the gap between Graph Databases and Large Language Models&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;AI summarizes the project documentation: &lt;a href="https://deepwiki.com/apache/hugegraph-ai"&gt;Ask DeepWiki&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="-overview"&gt;🎯 Overview&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;HugeGraph-LLM is a comprehensive toolkit that combines the power of graph databases with large language models.&#10;It enables seamless integration between HugeGraph and LLMs for building intelligent applications.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>HugeGraph-ML</title><link>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/hugegraph-ml/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/hugegraph-ml/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;HugeGraph-ML integrates HugeGraph with popular graph learning libraries, enabling end-to-end machine learning workflows directly on graph data.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="overview"&gt;Overview&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;&lt;code&gt;hugegraph-ml&lt;/code&gt; provides a unified interface for applying graph neural networks and machine learning algorithms to data stored in HugeGraph. It eliminates the need for complex data export/import pipelines by seamlessly converting HugeGraph data to formats compatible with leading ML frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="key-features"&gt;Key Features&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Direct HugeGraph Integration&lt;/strong&gt;: Query graph data directly from HugeGraph without manual exports&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;21 Implemented Algorithms&lt;/strong&gt;: Comprehensive coverage of node classification, graph classification, embedding, and link prediction&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DGL Backend&lt;/strong&gt;: Leverages Deep Graph Library (DGL) for efficient training&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;End-to-End Workflows&lt;/strong&gt;: From data loading to model training and evaluation&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Modular Tasks&lt;/strong&gt;: Reusable task abstractions for common ML scenarios&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="prerequisites"&gt;Prerequisites&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Python&lt;/strong&gt;: 3.9+ (standalone module)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HugeGraph Server&lt;/strong&gt;: 1.0+ (recommended: 1.5+)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UV Package Manager&lt;/strong&gt;: 0.7+ (for dependency management)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="installation"&gt;Installation&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="1-start-hugegraph-server"&gt;1. Start HugeGraph Server&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-0" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="bash" data-td-line-count="5"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-0-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Option 1: Docker (recommended)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;docker run -itd --name&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;hugegraph -p 8080:8080 hugegraph/hugegraph&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Option 2: Binary packages&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# See https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/download/download/&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="2-clone-and-setup"&gt;2. Clone and Setup&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-1" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="bash" data-td-line-count="2"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-1-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;git clone https://github.com/apache/hugegraph-ai.git&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; hugegraph-ai/hugegraph-ml&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="3-install-dependencies"&gt;3. Install Dependencies&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-2" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="bash" data-td-line-count="5"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-2-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# uv sync automatically creates .venv and installs all dependencies&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;uv sync&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Activate virtual environment&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;source&lt;/span&gt; .venv/bin/activate&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="4-navigate-to-source-directory"&gt;4. Navigate to Source Directory&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-3" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="bash" data-td-line-count="1"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-bb267603-fence-3-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;cd&lt;/span&gt; ./src&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-callout td-callout--note" role="note"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-callout__title"&gt;&lt;i class="td-callout__icon fa-solid fa-circle-info" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span class="td-callout__label"&gt;Note&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-callout__body"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;All examples assume you&amp;rsquo;re in the activated virtual environment.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Configuration Reference</title><link>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/config-reference/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/config-reference/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;This document provides a comprehensive reference for all configuration options in HugeGraph-LLM.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="configuration-files"&gt;Configuration Files&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Environment File&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;.env&lt;/code&gt; (created from template or auto-generated)&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prompt Configuration&lt;/strong&gt;: &lt;code&gt;src/hugegraph_llm/resources/demo/config_prompt.yaml&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-callout td-callout--tip" role="note"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-callout__title"&gt;&lt;i class="td-callout__icon fa-solid fa-lightbulb" aria-hidden="true"&gt;&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span class="td-callout__label"&gt;Tip&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-callout__body"&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Run &lt;code&gt;python -m hugegraph_llm.config.generate --update&lt;/code&gt; to auto-generate or update configuration files with defaults.&lt;/p&gt;&#10; &lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 id="environment-variables-overview"&gt;Environment Variables Overview&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="1-language-and-model-type-selection"&gt;1. Language and Model Type Selection&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-4bade1cf-fence-0" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="bash" data-td-line-count="13"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-4bade1cf-fence-0-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Prompt language (affects system prompts and generated text)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;LANGUAGE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;EN &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Options: EN | CN&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# LLM Type for different tasks&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;CHAT_LLM_TYPE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;openai &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Chat/RAG: openai | litellm | ollama/local&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;EXTRACT_LLM_TYPE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;openai &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Entity extraction: openai | litellm | ollama/local&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;TEXT2GQL_LLM_TYPE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;openai &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Text2Gremlin: openai | litellm | ollama/local&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Embedding type&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;EMBEDDING_TYPE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;openai &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Options: openai | litellm | ollama/local&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Reranker type (optional)&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;RERANKER_TYPE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Options: cohere | siliconflow | (empty for none)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h3 id="2-openai-configuration"&gt;2. OpenAI Configuration&#10;&lt;/h3&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Each LLM task (chat, extract, text2gql) has independent configuration:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>GraphRAG UI Details</title><link>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/quick_start/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/quick_start/</guid><description>&lt;blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Follow up &lt;a href="https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/"&gt;main doc&lt;/a&gt; to introduce the basic UI function &amp;amp; details, welcome to update and improve at any time, thanks&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;/blockquote&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="1-core-logic-of-the-project"&gt;1. Core Logic of the Project&#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="build-rag-index-responsibilities"&gt;Build RAG Index Responsibilities:&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Split and vectorize text&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Extract text into a graph (construct a knowledge graph) and vectorize the vertices&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="graphrag--user-functions-responsibilities"&gt;(Graph)RAG &amp;amp; User Functions Responsibilities:&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;ul&gt;&#10;&lt;li&gt;Retrieve relevant content from the constructed knowledge graph and vector database based on the query to supplement the prompt.&lt;/li&gt;&#10;&lt;/ul&gt;&#10;&lt;h1 id="2-processing-flow-build-rag-index"&gt;2. (Processing Flow) Build RAG Index&#10;&lt;/h1&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Construct a knowledge graph, chunk vector, and graph vid vector from the text.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>REST API Reference</title><link>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/rest-api/</link><pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://hugegraph.apache.org/docs/quickstart/hugegraph-ai/rest-api/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;HugeGraph-LLM provides REST API endpoints for integrating RAG and Text2Gremlin capabilities into your applications.&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="base-url"&gt;Base URL&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-0dde2d7b-fence-0" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="" data-td-line-count="1"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-0dde2d7b-fence-0-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0"&gt;&lt;code&gt;http://localhost:8001&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Change host/port as configured when starting the service:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-0dde2d7b-fence-1" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="bash" data-td-line-count="1"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-0dde2d7b-fence-1-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;python -m hugegraph_llm.demo.rag_demo.app --host 127.0.0.1 --port &lt;span class="m"&gt;8001&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;h2 id="authentication"&gt;Authentication&#10;&lt;/h2&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Currently, the API supports optional token-based authentication:&lt;/p&gt;&#10;&lt;div class="td-code td-code--untitled" id="td-code-0dde2d7b-fence-2" data-td-code data-td-code-auto-id&#10; data-td-language="bash" data-td-line-count="4"&gt;&#10; &lt;div class="td-code__viewport" id="td-code-0dde2d7b-fence-2-viewport" data-td-code-viewport&gt;&lt;div class="highlight"&gt;&lt;pre tabindex="0" class="chroma"&gt;&lt;code class="language-bash" data-lang="bash"&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="c1"&gt;# Enable authentication in .env&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;ENABLE_LOGIN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="nb"&gt;true&lt;/span&gt;&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;USER_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;your-user-token&#10;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="line"&gt;&lt;span class="cl"&gt;&lt;span class="nv"&gt;ADMIN_TOKEN&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class="o"&gt;=&lt;/span&gt;your-admin-token&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/pre&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;/div&gt;&#10;&lt;p&gt;Pass tokens in request headers:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>